{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Ced4QDuR7N8r2zwPBwKG2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This confirms it: `flags: Flags = flags` aliases `jupyter_server.serverapp.flags` directly instead of copying it, so the two mutations that follow leak `expose-app-in-browser` and `custom-css` into the shared upstream `serverapp_flags` dict — polluting every other `ServerApp`-based application in the process, not just `JupyterNotebookApp`. The test is correctly catching a real bug. Fixing it properly:"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":775,"cache_read_input_tokens":44025,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":775},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"54e9d7c1-1345-5e2d-ba67-93201e1134e8","uuid":"e20d3ac1-3408-4a62-9271-0a24d57e21af","timestamp":"2026-09-01T16:46:58.816Z","request_id":"req_011Ced4QDJwrDxPgcFkk9oQX"}
