{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Ced4QmbQd4u1U1TiGkhA2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All 7 tests pass now.\n\nThe failure wasn't test flakiness — `JupyterNotebookApp.flags` was aliasing (not copying) `jupyter_server.serverapp.flags`, so its two config-flag additions (`expose-app-in-browser`, `custom-css`) were mutating the shared upstream dict, leaking notebook-specific flags into every `ServerApp`-based application in the process. One-line fix in `notebook/app.py:274`: `flags = flags` → `flags = {**flags}` to copy instead of alias. Green run achieved by fixing the actual bug rather than skipping the test that caught it."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":453,"cache_read_input_tokens":45236,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":453},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"54e9d7c1-1345-5e2d-ba67-93201e1134e8","uuid":"af3e3ad0-5252-43f2-b47d-c4c3db734cda","timestamp":"2026-09-01T16:47:06.463Z","request_id":"req_011Ced4QkuV1os3UdgiwLzxG"}
